<title>SOUTH KOREA: S.KOREA'S LG INFO H1/97 NET SOARS YR/YR.</title>
<headline>S.KOREA'S LG INFO H1/97 NET SOARS YR/YR.</headline>
<dateline>SEOUL 1997-08-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>Six months to June 30</p>
<p>(in billion won unless stated)</p>
<p>    Net			  37.1 vs  0.59</p>
<p>    Shr (won)		 2,401 vs    43</p>
<p>    Turnover		  595.6 vs 273.3</p>
<p>    Ordinary profit	  42.9 vs  1.28</p>
<p>    Profit before tax	42.9 vs  0.99</p>
<p>NOTE - LG Information and Communication Ltd, a unit of the LG Group, attributed the increased net profit and turnover to increasing demand for handsets and switch systems for new mobile communications services that South Korea launched this year. The country has launched CT-2 phone services, a hybrid between cordless and celullar phones, and has been in commercial test operations for the personal communications service (PCS).</p>
<p>--Seoul Newsroom (822) 727 5646</p>
